  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nThe gradual cooling trend will continue through the long-term period \nas the high pressure aloft over the Four Corners region continues to \nweaken. Temperatures will generally be near normal, perhaps even \nleaning below normal to end the week. Troughing will begin to deepen \nnear the west coast through the start of the period, putting the \narea under southwest flow aloft. This will allow for monsoonal\nmoisture to begin creeping north across our area again. Chances\nfor showers and thunderstorms will increase near the ID/NV \nborder as early as Wednesday, before expanding north with each \npassing day. By Thursday, ensemble mean PWAT values reach the \n85-90th percentile in our southern zones. With those values \nencompassing our entire area come Saturday.",
